    <briefdescription>
<para>The out-of-plane parts of the tangent of a 2D material point with respect to the increment of the deformation gradient, which the hoop terms of an axisymmetric particle need (the out-of-plane stretch <formula id="238">$ F_{33} $</formula> is the hoop stretch there). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>With <formula id="239">$ \boldsymbol{F} = \Delta\boldsymbol{F}\,\boldsymbol{F}_n $</formula>,  <formula id="240">$ \partial F_{iI} / \partial
\Delta F_{jJ} = \delta_{ij}\, F_{n,JI} $</formula>, and a block-diagonal 2D state (no out-of-plane shear),     <formula id="241">\[  \frac{\partial \tau_{ij}}{\partial \Delta F_{33}} = \frac{\partial \tau_{ij}}{\partial F_{3I}}\, F_{n,3I},
  \qquad
  \frac{\partial \tau_{33}}{\partial \Delta F_{kL}} = \frac{\partial \tau_{33}}{\partial F_{kI}}\, F_{n,LI} .
\]</formula> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
